# Instantly Email Monitor — crontab entries
#
# Install on your server:
#   crontab -e
#   Paste the lines below (adjust the path to your project directory).
#
# To view current crontab:  crontab -l
# To edit:                  crontab -e
#
# IMPORTANT: Use absolute paths everywhere — cron runs with a minimal $PATH.
# Replace /home/user/email-monitor with the actual path to this project.
# Replace /usr/bin/python3 with the output of: which python3

# Load .env automatically (cron does not source shell profiles)
BASH_ENV=/home/user/email-monitor/.env
SHELL=/bin/bash

# Hourly check + auto-reconnect (runs at minute 0 of every hour)
0 * * * *   cd /home/user/email-monitor && /usr/bin/python3 monitor.py >> /var/log/email-monitor.log 2>&1

# Daily Slack report at 9:00 AM UTC (runs check first, then posts report)
0 9 * * *   cd /home/user/email-monitor && /usr/bin/python3 monitor.py --report >> /var/log/email-monitor.log 2>&1

# ── Railway.app deployment (alternative to cron) ─────────────────────────────
#
# Create TWO Railway cron services from the same repo / Docker image:
#
# Service 1 — "email-monitor-hourly"
#   Start command : python monitor.py
#   Cron schedule : 0 * * * *
#
# Service 2 — "email-monitor-daily"
#   Start command : python monitor.py --report
#   Cron schedule : 0 9 * * *
#
# Set all env vars (SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL, GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID, etc.) in the
# Railway dashboard under each service's Variables tab.
